## 🐞 Detailed Description of the Problem

**Current:** asking for the provenance or the diff of an artifact version that does not exist answers **500 `{"error":"Internal server error"}`** and writes an `unclassified_request_error` line to the API log. The sibling route for the same missing version answers **404 `Artifact version not found`**:

```
GET /api/sessions/<session>/artifact-versions/<missing>/content     → 404 {"error":"Artifact version not found"}
GET /api/sessions/<session>/artifact-versions/<missing>/provenance  → 500 {"error":"Internal server error"}
GET /api/sessions/<session>/artifact-versions/<missing>/diff        → 500 {"error":"Internal server error"}
```

**Expected:** a version id that does not exist is a client error on every artifact route — 404 with the same body the `content` route returns — so the Artifact modal can say the version is gone instead of showing "Internal server error", and the server log stops reporting a server fault for a plain bad id.

### Where

`services/api/src/http/index.ts` (read on `main` `89cd2d30c93e11c6e98e264cc08b171f6a3705f0`, blob `910ca85a4ae3`). The `content` route checks the version first:

```ts
// :3353-3359
const artifactVersionContentMatch = url.pathname.match(/^\/api\/sessions\/([^/]+)\/artifact-versions\/([^/]+)\/content$/);
if (artifactVersionContentMatch && request.method === "GET") {
  const version = store.getArtifactVersion(artifactVersionContentMatch[1]!, artifactVersionContentMatch[2]!);
  if (!version) return sendError(response, 404, "Artifact version not found");
  ...
```

but the `provenance` and `diff` routes (`:3360-3381`) call their helpers directly, with no existence check:

```ts
if (artifactVersionProvenanceMatch && request.method === "GET") {
  sendJson(response, 200, await artifactVersionProvenance(store, provenanceRecorder, memoryGraphClient,
    artifactVersionProvenanceMatch[1]!, artifactVersionProvenanceMatch[2]!));
```

Those helpers throw a plain `Error`, not an `ApiStatusError` and not a `SessionStoreHttpError`:

- `services/api/src/artifacts/index.ts:169` — `if (!version) throw new Error("Artifact version not found");` (blob `2d9539265751`)
- `services/api/src/artifacts/index.ts:349` — `if (!to) throw new Error("Artifact version not found");` (the `?against=` id on the diff route)

Nothing downstream recognises that message, so the top-level catch falls through to its last branch: `isKnownClientInputError` (`services/api/src/http/error-classification.ts:20`, blob `38b0b962dac9`) only matches `is required` / `must` / `unknown value` / `cannot` / `does not match` / `invalid` / `unsafe … path|archive|package` / `plain basename`, and the 404 message regex in `http/index.ts:3924` only covers `Project|Session|Proxy server|Provider|Model not found` and `Execution|Transfer|Timer|Subagent not found: …`. `Artifact version not found` matches neither → 500 `Internal server error` + `apiLog.error("unclassified_request_error", …)`.

User impact: a stale artifact link, a version deleted by retention, or a diff against a version that no longer exists is reported as a server failure. The Artifact modal reads content and provenance together (`apps/web/src/ScientificArtifacts.tsx:686`), so this is also the status a reader sees when the version is simply gone.

